---
import FocusedServicePage from '../components/FocusedServicePage.astro';
const data={
 slug:'international-seo-services',name:'International SEO Services',metaTitle:'International SEO Services | Market Expansion | Bright Forge',description:'International SEO for English-language markets. Country research, page ownership and regional technical checks. Discuss your expansion before building.',
 heroTitle:'International SEO That Gives <span>Each Market a Clear Role</span>',cta:'Discuss Your Market Expansion',
 intro:['Selling into another country does not mean copying the website and changing its currency. We identify the searches, products and pages that belong to each market, then plan the technical and content work around those differences.','Our Philippines-based team supports English-language expansion across markets including the UK, US, Australia and New Zealand. This service is for businesses expanding their own search footprint, not simply looking for an agency located overseas.'],
 proofTitle:'Regional Store Experience,',proofHighlight:'With Published Work to Review',
 proofBody:['Our published Speediance work covers UK, Australian and New Zealand storefronts. Those campaigns provide relevant experience of marketing related products to different country audiences. Each case should be read in its own market and reporting period.','A reported increase in clicks does not establish that one tag or technical change caused it. We use the work to show the type of business and regional challenge we have handled, while your own diagnosis determines the next recommendation.'],
 proofLinks:[{href:'/case-studies/speediance-uk-fitness-seo/',label:'Speediance UK'},{href:'/case-studies/speediance-au-fitness-seo/',label:'Speediance Australia'},{href:'/case-studies/speediance-nz-fitness-seo/',label:'Speediance New Zealand'}],
 sections:[
  {id:'market-and-page-plan',eyebrow:'Before New Pages',title:'Choose the Market,',highlight:'Then the Page',body:['We begin with what you can sell or deliver in each country. Availability, service boundaries, currency, buying questions and competition can change the search opportunity. A large keyword estimate is not enough to justify a new market or a duplicate page.'],rows:[{title:'Country-Specific Research',body:'We compare relevant competitors and queries in the intended country. Searcher location is kept separate from words in the query, so overseas interest in your home-market service is not mistaken for local-market demand.'},{title:'Existing Page Ownership',body:'We map which pages already meet the intent before proposing additions. The output distinguishes an existing owner to strengthen, a regional variant with a real purpose and an opportunity to defer.'},{title:'Commercial Priorities',body:'We prioritise pages connected to a viable offer and enquiry or purchase path. Translation, stock, legal requirements and delivery constraints need resolving before a campaign can promise to serve a new audience.'}],links:[{href:'/keyword-research-services/',label:'Keyword and competitor research'},{href:'/seo-audit-services/',label:'Existing-site audit'}]},
  {id:'regional-architecture',eyebrow:'Technical Ownership',title:'Make Regional Versions',highlight:'Understandable to Search Engines',body:['We review the country URL structure, internal links, canonical relationships and reciprocal hreflang annotations where regional equivalents exist. A missing return tag, a canonical pointing at the wrong storefront and a genuine duplicate require different fixes.','A country-code domain can be a strong market signal. A generic domain can support a different structure, but moving domains introduces its own risk. We compare options against your existing visibility and operating needs rather than prescribe a migration as a shortcut.'],rows:[{title:'One Site or Several Stores',body:'Document which pages are equivalent, which offer different products and which should remain unique. Do not force regional tags onto unrelated pages merely because they share a service label.'},{title:'Implementation and Verification',body:'The handover states the affected URLs, recommended changes and checks. We inspect released pages and regional links; implementation success and later search performance are reported separately.'}],links:[{href:'/technical-seo-services-philippines/',label:'Technical SEO implementation'},{href:'/website-migration-services/',label:'Migration risk and launch support'}]},
  {id:'market-content-and-measurement',eyebrow:'Content and Measurement',title:'Keep Local Relevance',highlight:'and Results Specific',body:['We adapt English-language content to the market: the actual offer, terminology, purchasing questions and supporting proof. Country-name substitutions and fabricated local offices do not help buyers decide. Where local-language production is required, that capability must be separately scoped rather than implied.','Measurement combines country-filtered Search Console data, agreed country queries and page ownership. We separate branded demand, broad discovery and commercial pages. Enquiries or sales are reported where reliable tracking connects them; impressions are not presented as revenue.'],links:[{href:'/ecommerce-seo-services/',label:'Multi-market ecommerce support'},{href:'/seo-services-new-zealand/',label:'SEO for New Zealand businesses'},{href:'/seo-services-uk/',label:'SEO for UK businesses'},{href:'/seo-services-usa/',label:'SEO for US businesses'},{href:'/seo-services-australia/',label:'SEO for Australian businesses'}]},
  {id:'international-handover',eyebrow:'What You Receive',title:'A Market Plan Your Team',highlight:'Can Implement and Review',body:['An agreed engagement can include the priority market and query map, existing and proposed page owners, regional architecture findings, content requirements and an implementation sequence. Each action should identify its dependency and how the completed work will be checked.','Send the website, target countries, store or service structure and any planned launches. We will identify the decisions needed before setting scope. This does not require building every country at once, and there is no guaranteed date for ranking in a new market.']}
 ],
 faqs:[
  {question:'Is this a translation service?',answer:'No. The offer described here covers English-language market research, page planning, technical regional checks and measurement. Translation or native-language production would require a separately confirmed scope and qualified resources.'},
  {question:'Do we need a separate domain for every country?',answer:'Not necessarily. We assess the current domain, regional offer, existing visibility and operational needs. Separate domains increase maintenance and can divide authority. A country structure should solve a real business and search requirement.'},
  {question:'Will hreflang make us rank internationally?',answer:'Hreflang can help search engines identify appropriate regional or language versions. It does not replace useful content, technical accessibility, relevant authority or a viable offer, and it does not guarantee rankings.'},
  {question:'Can you work with our developer?',answer:'Yes. We can prepare the regional page map and technical acceptance criteria, then review the released implementation. Responsibilities, access and release approval are agreed before changes are made.'},
  {question:'How is this different from your country service pages?',answer:'Our country pages explain SEO delivery for a business buying in that market. International SEO addresses one business expanding its own website across several markets, including the relationships between its country pages and how each market is measured.'}
 ]
};
---
<FocusedServicePage data={data} />
